./basis-of-design.md:239:### 7.1 Events are the atomic unit, and the log is append-only
./basis-of-design.md:241:All conversation and agent activity is represented as a stream of typed **Events**. The principal event types `[OH: ActionEvent/ObservationEvent/MessageEvent/AgentErrorEvent/Condensation]`:
./basis-of-design.md:248:- **ConversationErrorEvent / status events** — lifecycle signals (e.g., max-iterations reached, stuck).
./basis-of-design.md:252:- **Replay & resume:** the full state is reconstructed by replaying events. Close the tab, reopen, rehydrate — for free.
./basis-of-design.md:258:An `EventStore` interface supports filtering by kind/timestamp, sorting, and pagination, with a filesystem/SQLite implementation for v1 and the door open to object storage / Postgres `[OH: filesystem/aws/gcloud implementations behind one interface]`. History endpoints are paginated queries against this store; that is also the replay mechanism.
./basis-of-design.md:264:- We never delete events. To "forget," we append a **Condensation tombstone** that records *what to forget and what summary to insert in its place* (conceptually identical to Cassandra/Kafka tombstones).
./basis-of-design.md:283:- **REST** provides convenience message-send (a thin proxy) and history/replay (paginated `EventStore` queries).
./basis-of-design.md:440:Checked **every iteration**; on detection, set STUCK and stop. Scans only the **last ~20 events** (never materializes huge histories) and **resets after the last user message** (a new instruction = not stuck). Five patterns `[OH: stuck_detector.py, re-implemented]`:
./basis-of-design.md:597:The append-only event log (§7.1) is the audit trail. Security-relevant events (risk scores, confirmations, overflow calls, egress grants, kill-switch activations) are first-class events, queryable as a view.
./basis-of-design.md:603:- **Metrics:** per-run token/cost (local vs overflow), iteration counts, stuck-detection fires, condensation events, retrieval latency and source counts, citation-verification pass rates.
./basis-of-design.md:640:**Goal:** the four-package structure exists and a trivial agent loop runs end to end on the local-process sandbox, with events streaming to a minimal UI.
./basis-of-design.md:642:- Implement the **event model + filesystem/SQLite EventStore** (§7.1–7.2).
