./docs/archive/backlog-6-16-26-unaudited.md:371:**Exploit:** user visits any malicious site while the app runs; its JS hits `http://127.0.0.1:8000` cross-origin: `GET /conversations` + `/events` (read every conversation's full log/workspace), `/api/projects/{id}/download` (pull zips), `POST .../messages` (inject into a running agent), `POST .../files` (plant files), `.../kill`, `DELETE /api/projects/{id}`, `POST .../schedules` (persistent cron). With `allow_credentials=False` + `*`, the browser lets the attacker page read every response → full cross-origin read+write, not blind CSRF.
